    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d33">

                <pb facs="0128" n="882" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v02/pg882"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/5426</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Sharp</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-20T16:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 20, 1917, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 11.10 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2213. Referring to my despatch of May 4, 5410,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d33-f1"/>
                    relative to the various French committees blockade. I have just received from
                    the Minister of Foreign Affairs a note expressing the hope that the Federal
                    Government would designate a representative to the Permanent International
                    Committee of Economic Action.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sharp</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
